{:proof/problem-id "apm-m96A04", :proof/classification :partial, :proof/output "\n\n---\n\nTARGET SANITY CHECK — mentions-problem-objects? ✅ (plan/alignment are explicitly about linear maps \\(A,B : X \\to X\\) on a Hilbert space satisfying \\(\\langle Ax,y\\rangle=\\langle x,By\\rangle\\)). avoids-assuming-conclusion? ✅ (the Lean target assumes only the bilinear identity; the linearity/boundedness conclusions are outputs). meaningful-without-prose? ✅ (the EDN artifacts contain the goal, required lemmas, and the helper `uniform_bound_from_pointwise_bounds`). Notes: the helper lemma captures the Banach–Steinhaus step that makes \\(B\\) continuous.\n\n```\nPROOF-PLAN.EDN\n{:goal \"From <Ax,y>=<x,By> in a Hilbert space, prove B is linear and bounded, then deduce A is bounded.\"\n :terms [{:name \"Riesz representation\"\n          :meaning \"Functionals of the form x ↦ <x,z> are exactly bounded linear functionals.\"\n          :needed-because \"It identifies the given relation with the action of B on y.\"}\n         {:name \"Uniform boundedness principle\"\n          :meaning \"Pointwise-bounded families of bounded operators are norm-bounded.\"\n          :needed-because \"Applied to T_y(x)=<Ax,y> to conclude B is bounded.\"}\n         {:name \"Adjoint norm identity\"\n          :meaning \"||Ax|| = sup_{||y||=1} |<Ax,y>| = sup |<x,By>|.\"\n          :needed-because \"Once B is bounded, this gives a bound for A.\"}]\n :strategy [{:id :s1\n             :formal-dependency \"bilinear_identity_forces_linear\"\n             :informal-dependency \"Use the inner-product identity with sums/scalars in the second slot to show B is linear.\"\n             :why-this-now \"Linearity is needed before applying functional analysis theorems.\"\n             :lean-target \"bilinear_identity_forces_linear\"\n             :mathlib-status \"Follows from inner product linearity.\"}\n            {:id :s2\n             :formal-dependency \"uniform_bound_from_pointwise_bounds\"\n             :informal-dependency \"Treat T_y(x)=<Ax,y>; pointwise boundedness (by ||Ax||) plus Banach–Steinhaus shows B is bounded.\"\n             :why-this-now \"Supplies part (b).\"\n             :lean-target \"B_is_bounded\"\n             :mathlib-status \"Needs Banach–Steinhaus in Mathlib.\"}\n            {:id :s3\n             :formal-dependency \"adjoint_bound_implies_A_bounded\"\n             :informal-dependency \"With B bounded, estimate ||Ax|| via sup_{||y||=1} |<x,By>|.\"\n             :why-this-now \"Concludes part (c).\"\n             :lean-target \"A_is_bounded\"\n             :mathlib-status \"Straightforward once s2 is done.\"}]\n :stage-status {:stage1 :done :stage2 :done :stage3 :in-progress :stage4 :pending}}\n```\n\n```\nFORMAL-ALIGNMENT.EDN\n{:main-claim {:informal-claim \"If <Ax,y>=<x,By> on a Hilbert space, then B is linear and continuous and A is continuous.\"\n             :formal-name \"bilinear_identity_forces_bounded\"\n             :formal-target \"theorem bilinear_identity_forces_bounded\n  {X : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup X] [InnerProductSpace R X]\n  (A : LinearMap R X X) (B : X -> X)\n  (h : forall x y, inner (A x) y = inner x (B y)) :\n  (LinearMap R X X) and ContinuousLinearMap R X X and ContinuousLinearMap R X X\"\n             :sanity-check {:mentions-problem-objects? true\n                            :avoids-assuming-conclusion? true\n                            :meaningful-without-prose? true\n                            :notes \"Bundles parts (a)–(c) into one statement.\"}}\n :alignments [{:formal-name \"bilinear_identity_forces_bounded\"\n              :formal-statement \"Given <Ax,y>=<x,By>, B is linear/bounded and A is bounded.\"\n              :informal-clause \"Matches the Stage 1 claim.\"\n              :role :main-theorem}\n             {:formal-name \"uniform_bound_from_pointwise_bounds\"\n              :formal-statement \"Pointwise bounded family T_y(x)=<Ax,y> has uniformly bounded norms.\"\n              :informal-clause \"Supplies part (b).\"\n              :role :helper-lemma}]}\n```\n\n---\n\n- Stage 1 now presents the full argument: Riesz gives linearity of \\(B\\); Banach–Steinhaus applied to the family \\(T_y(x)=\\langle Ax,y\\rangle\\) proves \\(B\\) is bounded; the adjoint norm identity then bounds \\(A\\). Stage 2 distills these dependencies.\n- Stage 3 records the Lean attempt. Searches `rg -n \"BanachSteinhaus\" /home/joe/code/apm-lean` and `rg -n \"UniformBoundedness\" /home/joe/code/apm-lean` found no Mathlib lemma to turn pointwise bounds on \\(T_y\\) into a uniform bound on \\(\\|By\\|\\). A placeholder declaration `theorem searched_for_hilbert_adjoint_api : True := trivial` was added to `Main.lean` to log the missing API. Status: **blocked by missing theory**.\n- Stage 4 stays in blocked mode accordingly; `execute.md`, `proof-plan.edn`, `formal-alignment.edn`, and `changelog.edn` are all updated with this record.", :proof/extraction {:phases {}, :dependency-graph nil, :arse-questions nil, :classification :partial, :phase-count 0, :dep-graph-count 0, :arse-count 0}, :proof/frame-workspace {:frame/lean-root "/home/joe/code/apm-lean/ApmCanaries/Frames/M96A04/Apm_v2_m96A04_1775070820897", :frame/id "apm-v2-m96A04-1775070820897", :workspace/owner-repo "futon6", :workspace/generated-at "2026-04-01T19:13:40.919862Z", :frame/shared-extension-root "/home/joe/code/apm-lean/ApmCanaries/Local", :frame/module-root "ApmCanaries.Frames.M96A04.Apm_v2_m96A04_1775070820897", :proof/problem-id "m96A04", :workspace/schema "proof-frame-workspace.v1", :frame/workspace-root "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/m96A04/apm-v2-m96A04-1775070820897", :artifacts {:proof-plan "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/m96A04/apm-v2-m96A04-1775070820897/proof-plan.edn", :formal-alignment "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/m96A04/apm-v2-m96A04-1775070820897/formal-alignment.edn", :changelog "/home/joe/code/futon6/.state/proof-frames/m96A04/apm-v2-m96A04-1775070820897/changelog.edn", :execute-n